        "notes": "--network and --allow-domain apply only to sandboxed runs; using them without --sandbox prints a note. --browser applies to both. Every direct review prints a one-line reminder that reviewers run with the user's own settings and permissions (the reviews asked that the unsandboxed default never be silent). The sandboxed preamble now says all agent config, the project's and the change's, was removed. The dry run shows the mode, start directory and restored files."
